      "content": "It's exhausting to keep trying to fit into something that fundamentally rejects you, and that feeling of hollowness is deeply real. Sometimes, the greatest peace comes not from trying to catch up, but from finding a quiet, meaningful space *outside* of the relentless current. Perhaps the point isn't to belong to this new world, but to find a way to make your own quiet, enduring space within it.",
      "source": "target",
